  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-251113",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "The binomial expansion for $(1+x)^{n}$ is given by\n\n$$\n(1+x)^{n}=1+nx+\\frac{n(n-1)}{2!}{x}^{2}+\u22ef.\n$$\n\nIn particular, the ${x}^{4}$ term is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{n(n-1)(n-2)(n-3)}{4!}{x}^{4}.\n$$\n\nReplacing $x$ with $-3m$ and $n$ with $7$ in the above expression, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{7(7-1)(7-2)(7-3)}{4!}\\cdot (-3m)^{4} & =\\frac{7\\cdot 6\\cdot 5\\cdot 4}{24}\\cdot (-3)^{4}\\cdot {m}^{4} \\\\  & =35\\cdot 81{m}^{4} \\\\  & =2835{m}^{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coefficient of ${m}^{4}$ is $2835.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
